"""Job categories and the roles inside them, in words a person outside tech understands.

The owner's request (2026-11-13): "I cannot see where to pick a category. Our goal is traffic: every category needs its own page
with text, or we have nothing to rank for." So the site has a two-level directory, like the big job sites:

    category (FAMILIES, page /categories/<slug>/)  ->  roles (ROLES in build.py + MORE_ROLES here, page /roles/<slug>/)

A role is a set of job titles: the pattern is matched against the title of a posting. Roles may overlap (a "Staff Backend Engineer"
is both a backend engineer and a staff engineer); categories are only a way to browse, so a role may sit in two of them.
Every role has one plain line (what a person in this job does) and a plural for sentences ("jobs for accountants").
A role gets a page when at least 20 open jobs match it; add a role here and the build does the rest.
"""

# (name, slug, pattern matched against the job title, plural for sentences, what a person in this job does[, "nt"])
